WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.400
Hello, and welcome to CaseTrace.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:08.560
This is a time-tracking program certified by Microsoft,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.380
and you can get it from the Microsoft Store — you click here, and CaseTrace downloads.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.500
I already have the program, so let me just start it up.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.640
Here we see the program and its features.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:29.480
It has Activities, Folder Time, Timeline, Dashboard and Unallocated Time.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.720
You can also have it in Danish if you choose Danish.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.700
Activities logs everything you do.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:44.200
For example, right now I'm in CaseTrace, and you can see

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:52.320
that gradually the program or window you have active

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:56.280
appears in here, and it updates itself automatically.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.320
And then we have Folder Time.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:08.140
Here you can add folders or remove folders.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.280
Up here you add, down here you remove.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.360
I've added a folder called Josefine.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.980
Then I can add a budget.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:25.760
I can enter that it's client number 25, and that I need 10 hours.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.640
And I charge 750 an hour, then we confirm it.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:34.600
Then we can see some figures appear here, showing how much time has been spent.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:40.680
The clever thing about this folder is that now I go into the Josefine folder,

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.140
and then I open a subfolder.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.340
Inside the folder there are two documents.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.720
I'll try opening one here, and then I'll try opening the other one here.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.040
So now I have two open.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.460
Of course only one can be active at a time.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.740
But now I have one open, and then I'll try having the other one open.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.240
Then we go back into the program here.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.600
Then we can refresh.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:11.240
Then we can see it has already recorded that I've spent a few seconds.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.700
For example 13 seconds in the folder, and how much I've spent on each file.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.160
What it then does is add the time up here.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:24.960
And then you can see how much time you've spent in total, on all the files in that folder and its subfolders.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.380
And how much money you've spent so far.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:37.680
I've also built a feature where you can share the folder.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.920
So you choose yourself which folder you want to share.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:46.800
If I share the Josefine folder, I can share it here, if this were a OneDrive.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.800
If you're on Business.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.740
If there are several of you working in the same folders in OneDrive, you can share it.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:59.940
And the clever part is that you can then see how many machines it's shared with.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:05.720
How much time has been spent in total, across the different computers.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.220
And then you can open Shared Time.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.500
Here it shows that 13 seconds have been spent in total.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.560
My name here is John. I can enter a different name.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.440
I can write Hanne and save it as that.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.160
Then the others who also use that folder can go in and see

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.400
how long you've spent on it.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.620
And you can see the others' time.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.900
And they can see your time.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.800
And you can see the total time for it.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.740
When, and how much.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.680
I've also built some reports you can pull here.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.600
For internal use, for example, you can choose the date.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.420
The period you want the report from.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.620
And then you can choose whether it should be chronological.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.060
So you can see how much time was spent per day.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.620
Per file — but that can get very long.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.880
Or you can choose the total.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.520
If I choose the total here.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:53.640
Then we can see.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.560
Client number 25 comes up.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.280
And the date I've chosen.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.700
Then you can see how much time you've spent.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.780
And how much money you've spent.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.620
And you can add your company logo.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.260
And whatever you're called.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.620
And then you can pull reports.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.660
Otherwise, you can go in and pull client reports.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.120
It's the same.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.080
And you can choose the same things in here.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.320
It looks slightly different.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.340
It can be attached as documentation.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:24.460
So clients can follow along with how much time you've spent.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.400
On files and so on.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:34.520
I forgot to mention that you can add notes in here.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.580
So we can write: test with the client.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.640
Or into Activities.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.360
If you do something out of the ordinary.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.720
Then you can write a note in there.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:48.220
No — test, erm.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.140
And you can also block things.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.060
If there's a program you don't want

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.540
it to track.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.900
Or a file.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:55.600
Or something.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:56.580
And then up in the menu.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:57.900
You can go into Files.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:58.920
Then you can go into Notes.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.780
And then you can see, for each day,

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.080
the notes that have been written.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.540
And change them.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.440
Or delete them.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.980
The same applies in Timeline.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.340
Or Timeline in here.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.880
It's simply broken down in detail.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:14.660
You can add notes here too.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.300
What you've done and spent the time on.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.240
You can go into,

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:19.640
for example, CaseTrace.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:20.220
There you can see

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.740
I've had something open 24 times.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:22.380
Then you can see

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:23.500
the time of day,

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:24.800
and how long.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:25.680
Simply,

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:26.680
across a whole day.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.760
So that's really useful.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.460
And you can go back in time.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.580
Or forward in time.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.160
And look.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.080
And then we have Dashboard.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.520
There's a chart

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.040
that shows

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.460
which browsers

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.660
you've used most today, and how many hours

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:43.120
you've spent

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:43.780
over the week.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:49.240
And various other information — and up here you can also

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.300
add time manually in Activities.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.480
If you're in a meeting.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:54.400
Or something special.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:55.440
That didn't get picked up.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:56.560
And you can add it

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:01.260
to a specific case under Folder Time, if

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.640
it's some program

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.900
it can't see

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:04.740
what you're doing in.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.840
And then we have the interesting one here, it's called

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:15.520
Unallocated Time — it simply tracks

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.200
everything over 30 seconds

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:18.340
you've spent time on

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.200
that isn't in

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:19.740
Folder Time.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:20.560
If it's some

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:21.200
particular program

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:22.160
that can't be

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.460
in Folder Time, but you'd like

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.360
to have it added

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:24.980
to your case.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:25.780
Then you can go in.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.160
And then you can

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.220
press assign.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:29.860
And then you can

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:33.380
drop it into the folder it belongs to — now I'll try

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.160
dropping it into Josefine.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:35.920
Then we go in

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:39.960
and look, and CaseTrace has been added to

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:40.980
Josefine.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:41.940
And then you can see

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:45.500
the time spent on it. The program can also do

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:47.660
a lot more things

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:48.980
that I can't manage

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.100
to go through in full, but

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:52.840
you can, for example,

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.280
look up a company registration number,

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:54.980
if you need to.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.740
When you start Windows every

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.220
day, the machine then comes up.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:11.380
It can send automatic emails every day or every

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:13.440
week about the time you've spent, and so

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.320
you get an overview. Now we can see here.
